    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1749">

                <pb facs="1418" n="1302" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg1302"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.0145/9.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé d’Affaires to the Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 641.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">St. Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1911-07-21">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 21, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to this Embassy’s dispatch
                    No. 592 of June 21 last, and to previous despatches on the subject of the law
                    extending the area of Russian territorial waters to twelve marine miles from
                    low-water mark along the Pacific coast of the Empire, I have the honor herewith
                    to forward (with translation) Law No. 1066 of the “Collection of Laws and
                    Dispositions of the Government,” establishing the regulations for sea-fishing in
                    the Maritime Government-Generalship.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Post Wheeler.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>




                <xi:include href="d1749-a1.xml" xpointer="d1749-a1"/>
